[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Report polling (frontend/lib/useReport.ts)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Poll sequence and back-off
STATEMENT: >>>
`pollReport(id, signal, onState, options)` asks `getStatus` at once, then after each answer waits `firstDelay`
(default 1,000 ms) and multiplies the wait by 1.5 (rounded to whole ms) up to `maxDelay` (default 5,000 ms). A
successful status call resets the count of failed calls. For a status other than `complete` or `failed` it reports
`queued` when `progress` is 0 or less and `processing` otherwise, with `progress`, `message` and `eta` (the
`eta_seconds` when it is a number of 0 or more, else null). For `complete` it calls `getReport`: a report gives
`done` with the report and ends; null (202) keeps polling with no state reported.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
COMMENT: >>>
HLR-WEB-003 says the browser polls first after 1 s. The poller asks at once when it starts (the server render has
just asked once); the first wait of 1 s comes after that first answer. Problem report PR-038.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Poll end states
STATEMENT: >>>
`pollReport` ends with exactly one final state: `failed` with the status's `error` (null when empty) when the
status is `failed`; `expired` when a call answers 404; `failed` when a call answers 422 or 500, with the server's
text or null when the server sent none; `error` after 5 failed calls in a row of any other kind (no connection,
time limit, another status); `stopped` when more than `maxWaitMs` (default 600,000 ms) has passed since the start,
checked before each status call. When `signal` is aborted it returns without reporting a state.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: useReport hook
STATEMENT: >>>
`useReport(id)` starts in `queued` with progress 0, an empty message and no time estimate. When `id` is given it
runs `pollReport` with a new abort signal, and again from `queued` whenever `id` changes or `retry()` is called; the
previous run is aborted then and when the component unmounts, and states that arrive after an abort are dropped.
Polling goes on while the browser tab is hidden.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The tests drive `pollReport` only; no test renders the hook. A review reads `useReport`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-003

