[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Numbers, times and units (frontend/lib/format.ts)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Missing values and plain numbers
STATEMENT: >>>
`DASH` is the long dash (U+2014). `isNum(v)` is true only for a finite number. `fmtNum(v, digits = 1, unit)` writes
`v` in the `en` number format with thousands separators and at most `digits` decimals, followed by a space and the
unit when one is given; `fmtFixed(v, digits, unit)` writes exactly `digits` decimals; `fmtInt(v, unit)` rounds to a
whole number first. Each returns `DASH` for null, undefined, NaN or an infinite value, never `0`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Scores and changes
STATEMENT: >>>
`fmtScore(v)` is `<v rounded to a whole number> / 100`. `fmtDelta(v, digits = 1, unit)` is `+` for a positive
value, the minus sign U+2212 for a negative one and `±` for 0, followed by `fmtNum` of the absolute value. Both
return `DASH` for a missing value.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
