[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter values
STATEMENT: >>>
`fmtParam(v)` writes a value that is not a finite number as `String(v)`, a whole number in full, and any other
value as the shortest decimal of `v` rounded to 7 significant digits. When that text would use exponent notation
it writes `v` with 10 decimals instead, without trailing zeros or a trailing point.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
COMMENT: >>>
HLR-WEB-025 asks for at most 7 significant digits and no exponent. A whole number is written with all its digits
(more than 7 when it has them), and a value below 1e-6 is written with 10 decimals, so it keeps fewer than 7
significant digits and one below 5e-11 is written as `0`. Problem report PR-039.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-025
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unit systems and conversion
STATEMENT: >>>
The unit systems are `metric`, `imperial` and `aviation` (`UNIT_SYSTEMS`, in that order); `isUnitSystem(v)` is
true only for one of these strings. `toUnit(v, quantity, system)` returns the value and unit: metric leaves the
value and gives `m` (altitude, distance), `m/s` (speed), `°C` (temperature); imperial gives feet (m / 0.3048),
`mph` (m/s x 3600 / 1609.344) and `°F` (°C x 9 / 5 + 32); aviation gives feet, `kt` (m/s x 3600 / 1852) and
`°C`. `fmtQty(v, quantity, system, digits = 1)` is `fmtNum` of the converted value with its unit, and `DASH` for a
missing value.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-021

