[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Chart data (frontend/lib/chartData.ts)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-046
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Common rules for chart series
STATEMENT: >>>
`chartSpecsFor(finding)` returns no chart when `chart_data` is not an object or the category is not one of
oscillation, vibration, battery, gps, ekf, motors. In a series an element that is not a finite number becomes
null (a gap, never 0), and a value that is not an array gives an empty series. For time charts the timestamps are
in ms and are shown in seconds (ms / 1000); only indices with a timestamp are kept; above 500 of them, 500 are kept
at `floor(k x n / 500)` for k = 0 to 499, the same indices for every series. A series with no value left is
dropped; with fewer than 2 points or no series left there is no chart.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oscillation spectrum
STATEMENT: >>>
For an oscillation finding the spectrum pairs `frequencies` and `amplitudes` up to the shorter length and keeps the
pairs whose frequency is a number (amplitudes may be gaps); with fewer than 2 pairs there is no chart. The chart
key is `oscillation:<axis>`, the title names the axis when `axis` is a string, and the peak is `peak_hz` when that
is a finite number, else none.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vibration charts
STATEMENT: >>>
For a vibration finding the sources are the object entries of `chart_data.instances` when that is an object, else
`chart_data` itself; at most the first three are drawn. A source with a `vibe` array gives one series against
reference lines at `warn` and `crit` (each when a finite number), in `rad/s` when its `metric` contains `gyro`
(case ignored) and in `m/s²` otherwise, keyed `vibration:<source name, else metric, else vibe>`. Any other source
gives the series `x`, `y` and `z` in `m/s²`, keyed `vibration:<source name>` and titled with that name when there
is one.
<<<
