[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Flight path geometry (frontend/components/three/flightPathGeometry.ts)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-058
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Path point limit
STATEMENT: >>>
`sampleIndices(n, max = 1000)` returns every index when `n` is at most `max`, and otherwise `max` indices
`round(k x (n - 1) / (max - 1))` for k = 0 to max - 1, so the first and the last point are always kept.
`MAX_PATH_POINTS` is 1,000.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-059
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Path in scene coordinates
STATEMENT: >>>
`buildFlightPathScene(path)` takes `[lat, lon, alt_m]` points and returns null for an empty path. Relative to the
first point, x is east in m (`(lon - lon0) x 111320 x cos(lat0)`), z is minus north in m (`(lat - lat0) x 111320`)
and y is the height above the lowest point times 3. All three are multiplied by one scale that makes the longer of
the x and z extents 3.2 units (an extent of 0 counts as 1 m), and x and z are centred on the middle of their
extents. It also returns `maxAltitudeM`, the highest minus the lowest altitude in m, and the scale. `minMax`
returns the lowest and highest value with a plain loop.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-WEB-060
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Path colours
STATEMENT: >>>
`normaliseValues(values)` is null for no values or no finite number, else each value's position from 0 (lowest)
to 1 (highest), with a span of 0 counted as 1 and null where a value is not a finite number. `rampColour(t)` clamps
`t` to 0 to 1 and interpolates linearly over the RGB stops (0.23, 0.32, 0.55), (0.13, 0.57, 0.55), (0.99, 0.91,
0.15). `buildPathColors(mode, values)` is null in `standard` mode or when there is nothing to normalise, and
otherwise one ramp colour per point, grey (0.45, 0.47, 0.50) where there is no reading. `rgbCss` writes
`rgb(r, g, b)` with each part times 255, rounded.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-WEB-008

